module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.handwritten_population_wrong_by_gain_and_by_loss

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data handwritten_population_wrong_by_gain_and_by_loss: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "handwritten_population_wrong_by_gain_and_by_loss" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a handwritten population can be wrong both by failing to gain a member and by failing to lose one. Completeness and liveness are the same derivation problem viewed in opposite directions.** (INVALID STATE: a join, gate, or census filters a live roster by a hand-authored identity list, and that list is treated as the waiter / subject / obligation population. Membership then moves only when an author edits the list. A real waiter never appended is invisible -- the join reports AllWaitersStanding over the identities it knows. A member that retired through another legitimate arm and was left on the list is stale -- the join reports SplitRetirement against a standing that the row's own trigger already authorised.",

    "HARM: omission is silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5), because nothing in the enrolled set is split. Staleness is loud but FALSE: it refuses a retirement the trigger still names. Either way the handwritten list is a second retirement gate, which DESIGN section 4b(3) forbids -- a drop is retired by its trigger and by nothing else.",

    "SPECIMEN (gunbc#10837, gunbc.rung_drop.shared_capability missing_cadence_category, review 62536). The join honestly declares current rung 2 over enrolled waiters only. WaiterAbsent is listed-but-absent, the opposite of unenrolled-but-waiting. floor_cut_falsifier_cadence is on the list because it waits on the same missing cadence, and also retires when an operator withdraws that capability. A static census of drops that mention missing_cadence_category would still list it after that withdrawal arm fires, reproducing SplitRetirement. The dual-arm delist sentence on the AuthoredProse trigger is diligence over the same handwritten list, not derivation.",

    "THE COMPOUND FORM OF THE SAME CLASS (review 62552): a row whose trigger is the shared capability AND a remainder. witness_deferral_freeze_forward_rule retires only on BOTH cadence (a) and required-run discovery-corpus (b); transitional_admission_exception retires when each named identity has a live scheduled route, which is more than the category existing. Joining them by whole-row standing forces either the pure waiters to stay Standing after the capability has fired, or the compounds to be marked Retired before their own triggers are satisfied. The repair on the handwritten list is the same delist as the withdrawal arm: when the capability fires and the remainder is still unsatisfied, the identity leaves waiter_identities in that change and stays Standing. active_waiters already names this -- a standing drop whose remaining unsatisfied condition no longer includes the capability is not a waiter.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `roster_is_its_own_denominator`. That class is a report that enumerates whatever the list happens to hold and presents it as an answer about the subject, with no independent expected set. Here an independent roster EXISTS (gunbc.rung_drop.roster) and the join reads standing from it; the defect is that FILTER MEMBERSHIP is still authored, so both gain and loss stay off the derivation. A second list plus set-equality against mention-of-the-capability is still two writable lists, which that neighbour's own trigger already refuses as a structural climb.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `selection_view_read_as_population`. Membership here does not move with a measured threshold. It moves when an author forgets to append, or forgets to delete.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder on the omission path -- an unenrolled waiter leaves AllWaitersStanding, so the enrolled witness cannot discriminate it. Split retirement among enrolled identities is a different path, already mechanically preventable by the same module's witness. DESIGN section 4b(1): a class's current rung is the minimum across its in-scope paths, so this row does not inherit the enrolled-split rung.",

    "CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: active_waiters(capability) = standing drops whose currently-unsatisfied retirement condition includes the capability. The join folds that derived set. Then omission is unwritable (a real waiter is in the fold without being listed) and staleness is unwritable (a drop whose remaining unsatisfied condition no longer includes the capability has left the fold). Sufficient for deleting waiter_identities as an authority. A static capability-reference census -- every drop that mentions the identity -- is not this trigger: it names less than the capability it restores (DESIGN section 4b(2)) and stays satisfied while a legitimately retired member still pollutes the population.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a population is a hand-authored list joined to a live roster, ask both what happens if a new waiter is never appended AND what happens if a member retires through an arm that is not the shared capability -- if either answer is silence or a false split, the list is the class.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "gunbc.rung_drop.shared_capability" as NonEmptyStr,
      decl_name: "missing_cadence_category" as NonEmptyStr,
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
  ],
}
